    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A sacred amulet that channels divine energy through aether, allowing clerics to store and cast spells through the power of prayer.</p>\n<h3>Sacred Slots</h3>\n<p>The Metatron holds five prayer slots, each a different form of sacred invocation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Supplication</strong> - A humble prayer of need</li>\n<li><strong>Invocation</strong> - A call upon divine power</li>\n<li><strong>Litany</strong> - A repeated prayer of devotion</li>\n<li><strong>Benediction</strong> - A blessing bestowed</li>\n<li><strong>Consecration</strong> - A prayer of sanctification</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Abilities</h3>\n<p><img src=\"modules/elysium/assets/icons/MetatronImprint.png\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;\"><strong>Prayer of Creation:</strong> Imprint any 1st level Cleric spell from the divine spell list into an empty slot. No aether cost.</p>\n<p><img src=\"modules/elysium/assets/icons/TheMetatron.png\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;\"><strong>Psalm of Casting:</strong> Cast a stored spell using aether fuel. Spend a spell slot to enhance: non-healing spells upcast to 2nd level; healing spells choose extended range (40ft), upcast, or maximum healing.</p>\n<p><img src=\"modules/elysium/assets/icons/MetatronForgetSpell.png\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;\"><strong>Meditation of Forgetfulness:</strong> Remove stored spells from slots.</p>\n<p><img src=\"modules/elysium/assets/icons/TheMetatron.png\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;\"><strong>Healer's Gambit:</strong> Cast Mass Healing Word (3rd level) using a 2nd level spell slot and aether. <em>Warning:</em> Gain 1 Aether Toxicity Level. Roll d20 - on failure (1 to 2+ATL*2), The Metatron goes dormant until long rest.</p>\n<p class=\"elysium-info-box\"><strong>Note:</strong> This modification requires attunement and a minimum cleric level of 3. Healer's Gambit becomes increasingly dangerous as Aether Toxicity accumulates.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
